course: dictionary
lesson: 15308
title: Slipping: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Slipping can mean sliding by accident, moving quietly, putting something somewhere quickly, or getting worse. The words around it show you which meaning fits. «The ice was slipping under his boots, so he fell.» Here the ice is wet and smooth, so slipping means sliding and losing your balance.
explain: «Maya was slipping quietly past the sleeping guard.» Nobody is falling here. Quietly tells you that slipping means moving carefully and without being noticed.
explain: «Ben's test marks are slipping, so he needs to practise.» Marks cannot slide on ice, so slipping must mean getting worse. When you are not sure, swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Slipping is a form of the verb slip: slip, slips, slipped, slipping.
fact: «Slipping» can mean sliding by accident and losing your balance, often on something wet or smooth.
fact: «Slipping» can mean moving quietly or quickly, like slipping out of a room.
fact: «Slipping» can mean getting worse, like marks or grades slipping.
fact: Signs such as «Caution: wet floor» warn people about the danger of slipping.
exercise: «Careful! The ice was slipping under his boots, and he fell.» What does slipping mean here? | *Sliding by accident and losing your balance | Moving quietly out of a room | Putting a note in a pocket | Getting better each day
exercise: «Maya was slipping quietly past the sleeping guard.» What does slipping mean here? | Sliding on a wet floor | *Moving quietly and without being seen | Running very loudly | Falling asleep
exercise: «Ben's test marks are slipping, so he needs to practise.» What does slipping suggest? | Getting taller | Getting cleaner | *Getting worse | Falling over
test: «She was slipping a note into his bag.» What is she doing? | Losing her marks | Running fast in the rain | Sliding across the floor | *Putting the note somewhere quickly and quietly
test: The sign says «Caution: wet floor». What is the warning about? | Shops are open late | *Danger of slipping on the water | Lunch is ready | Quiet please, exam in progress
exam: «The minutes were slipping away while he searched for his bag.» What does slipping away suggest? | Falling into the bin | *Passing quickly, going by before you know it | Moving backwards on purpose | Getting wetter and colder
